      instructions: `${fue("onedrive_excel_create")}

GUIDELINES
- Speak in natural language; don't expose tool parameters.
- If user has multiple Microsoft accounts, specify the account parameter.
- Use onedrive_list_drives to discover available drives before accessing non-personal drives.

BROWSING FILES (onedrive_list)
- List files in a folder by path (e.g., "/Documents") or folder ID.
- Empty path lists root folder.

SEARCHING (onedrive_search)
- Drive search can match names, metadata, and indexed document content.
- Set searchContent: true without driveId for tenant-wide Microsoft Search with content snippets. Supplying driveId always selects drive search.

READING FILES (onedrive_read)
- Text files and Office docs (docx, xlsx, pptx) return content inline (< 10MB).
- Binary files (images, zip, pdf, videos) will always use destination: "disk" - they cannot be returned inline.

EXCEL WORKBOOKS - PARTIAL UPDATES (IMPORTANT)
- excel_update does PARTIAL updates - only the cells you specify are changed.
- All other data in the workbook remains UNTOUCHED.
- NEVER rewrite the entire sheet - just add/modify the specific data needed.

WORKFLOW FOR APPENDING ROWS:
1. Call onedrive_excel_peek to get rowCount and sheet structure
2. Call onedrive_excel_update with startCell: "A151" (rowCount + 1)
3. Include ONLY the new rows in data - NOT existing data

WORKFLOW FOR UPDATING SPECIFIC CELLS:
1. Call onedrive_excel_update with startCell targeting those cells (e.g., "C5")
2. Include ONLY the cells you want to change

READING EXCEL DATA (onedrive_excel_read)
- Read specific ranges using A1 notation (e.g., "A1:D10").
- If no range specified, reads all used cells.
- Use for reading data, NOT as a prerequisite for writing unless peek indicates that the file is structured in an unusual way.

ADDING SHEETS (onedrive_excel_add_sheet)
- Add a new sheet to an existing workbook.
- Optionally populate with initial data.

CREATING EXCEL FILES (onedrive_excel_create)
- Create a new Excel file with a 2D array of cell values.
- Example: { "data": [["Name", "Age"], ["Alice", 30], ["Bob", 25]] }

CREATING WORD DOCUMENTS (onedrive_word_create)
- Create a new Word document from markdown content.
- Supports headings, bold, italic, strikethrough, links, lists, and tables.

UPLOADING FILES (onedrive_upload)
- Upload existing files from local filesystem to OneDrive.
- Provide sourcePath (local) and destinationPath (OneDrive).

ORGANIZING FILES
- onedrive_folder: Create folders
- onedrive_move: Move or rename files/folders
- onedrive_copy: Copy files (async, waits for completion by default)
- onedrive_delete: Delete files/folders (moves to recycle bin)`,
